# Code Style Rules

> Replace the examples below with your project's actual conventions.
> Delete any section that doesn't apply to your stack.

---

## Naming

- Variables and functions: `camelCase`
- Types and classes: `PascalCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Files: `kebab-case.ts`
- Database columns: `snake_case`

## Functions

- Prefer pure functions over side-effect-heavy ones
- Max function length: ~40 lines — extract if longer
- Single responsibility: one function does one thing

## Error handling

- Never swallow errors silently
- Always log the original error before rethrowing
- User-facing errors must go through a central error formatter

## Imports

- Group order: stdlib → third-party → internal
- No circular imports
- Prefer named exports over default exports

## Comments

- Explain **why**, not **what**
- TODO format: `// TODO(name): description` — always attributed
- No commented-out code in commits

